From: jarojarojaro-jaro <miki.jaroszek@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 19:04:40 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 15/54] CUDA/HIP: write the q8_1 MMVQ activations from the
 producing norm/GLU/unary*mul kernels

RMS_NORM*MUL, SWIGLU and UNARY*MUL kernels whose output feeds an MMVQ MUL_MAT also write the
q8_1 blocks (same arithmetic as quantize_q8_1) into the MMVQ activation cache, so the
consumer skips its quantize_q8_1 launch.

Qwen3.8-27B MTP n=4 verify graph (rocprofv3): 1308 -> 1052 kernels, gap sum 4.30 -> 3.50 ms,
verify wall 32.39 -> 31.62 ms. Greedy plain/MTP outputs identical.
Server spec_sweep Qwen UD (interleaved A/B x2): 37.73 -> 37.04 ms/step, 83.2 -> 84.9 t/s.
